# Theme elements: element

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:giggly, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "..")},
  {:kino, "~> 0.19"}
  ])
```

## About this notebook

This notebook follows the examples on ggplot2's reference page for
[`element()`](https://ggplot2.tidyverse.org/reference/element.html), which covers `margin()`,
`margin_part()`, `margin_auto()`, `element_blank()`, `element_rect()`, `element_line()`,
`element_text()`, `element_polygon()`, `element_point()`, `element_geom()` and `rel()` too, in the
order the page gives them. Each example shows ggplot2's code first and then Giggly's. An example
Giggly cannot draw yet keeps its ggplot2 code and names what it is waiting for, so the page is also
a list of what remains.

In ggplot2's theme system, the `element_` functions say how the parts of a plot that are not data
are drawn: `element_blank()` draws nothing and takes no space, `element_rect()` draws borders and
backgrounds, `element_line()` lines and `element_text()` text, and `element_geom()` sets the
defaults that layers draw with. `element_polygon()` and `element_point()` are not drawn in
standard plots and serve extensions. `rel()` gives a size relative to the parent element's, and
`margin()`, `margin_part()` and `margin_auto()` give the margins around an element. Giggly draws
every plot in ggplot2's default theme, `theme_gray()`, and has none of these yet: there is no way
to change the theme.

## Blank elements

```r
# A standard plot
plot <- ggplot(mpg, aes(displ, hwy)) + geom_point()

# Turning off theme elements by setting them to blank
plot + theme(
  panel.background = element_blank(),
  axis.text = element_blank()
)
```

Not in Giggly yet: changing the theme, here to remove the panel's background and the axes' tick
labels.

## Styling text

```r
# Text adjustments
plot + theme(
  axis.text = element_text(colour = "red", size = rel(1.5))
)
```

Not in Giggly yet: changing the theme, here to draw the tick labels in red at a size relative to
their parent element's, with `rel()`.

## An axis line with an arrow

```r
# Turning on the axis line with an arrow
plot + theme(
  axis.line = element_line(arrow = arrow())
)
```

Not in Giggly yet: changing the theme, here to draw each axis's line, ending in an arrow made by
`grid`'s `arrow()`.

## Backgrounds and margins

```r
plot + theme(
  panel.background = element_rect(fill = "white"),
  plot.margin = margin_auto(2, unit = "cm"),
  plot.background = element_rect(
    fill = "grey90",
    colour = "black",
    linewidth = 1
  )
)
```

`margin_auto(2, unit = "cm")` gives the same 2 cm margin on all four sides.

Not in Giggly yet: changing the theme, here to give the panel a white background, and the whole
plot a margin and a light grey background with a black border.

## Defaults for layers

```r
ggplot(mpg, aes(displ, hwy)) +
  geom_point() +
  geom_smooth(formula = y ~ x, method = "lm") +
  theme(geom = element_geom(
    ink = "red", accent = "black",
    pointsize = 1, linewidth = 2
  ))
```

Not in Giggly yet: `geom_smooth()`, formulas fitted by `lm()`, and `element_geom()`, which here
sets the colours, point size and line width the layers draw with.
